  https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/65ec61dde94ffa93342728d324fecf474d228e1f/packages/contracts-bedrock/contracts/universal/CrossDomainMessenger.sol#L398

  - After some time, the protocol notices that the distribution of incentives to instances A and B were failed. In other words, the tokens are transferred from L1 to `OptimismTargetDispenserL2` on L2, but the message is not delivered properly. So, DAO decides to solve this issue. Thus, DAO calls the function `processDataMaintenance` and provides the input data as: `targets = [instanceA], amounts = [90e18]` to skip the instanceB which was causing the issue. By doing so, the instanceA receives its portion.
  ```solidity
    function processDataMaintenance(bytes memory data) external {
